<header><p class="st-kicker">county · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">County of Besalú</h1><p class="st-meta">878 CE – 1111 CE (approx.) · capital Besalú</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Catalan county of the Garrotxa whose fortified bridge and Jewish quarter still mark the medieval town of Besalú.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/besalu">Besalú</a> emerged as a county in the later 9th century, carved out of the lands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/girona">Girona</a> and linked to the family of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wilfred-the-hairy">Wilfred the Hairy</a>. For much of the 10th century it was held together with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cerdanya">Cerdanya</a> by Wilfred's descendants, before acquiring its own line of counts.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its best-known count, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernat-i-count-of-besalu">Bernat I Tallaferro</a>, from 988 to 1020, was a brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oliba">Abbot Oliba</a> and briefly obtained a bishopric for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/besalu">Besalú</a> from the pope in 1017. The town grew around its castle, monasteries such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sant-pere-de-besalu">Sant Pere de Besalú</a>, a fortified bridge over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fluvia">Fluvià</a> and a Jewish community whose ritual bath survives. The economy was rural, with markets on the routes to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roussillon">Roussillon</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Count <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernat-iii-of-besalu">Bernat III</a> married a daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramon-berenguer-iii-of-barcelona">Ramon Berenguer III of Barcelona</a> and died without heirs in 1111, so the county passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a>. It became part of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/principality-of-catalonia">Catalonia</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/crown-of-aragon">Crown of Aragon</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/county-of-besalu.jpg" alt="County of Besalú" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: PolAloC · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:County_of_Besal%C3%BA_flag_reconstruction.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>878 CE – 1111 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>county</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Besalú</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Bernat I Tallaferro, Bernat III</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Latin</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/spain">Spain</a>, <a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Comtat de Besalú</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=994&amp;focus=county-of-besalu" aria-label="County of Besalú on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4746 676 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where County of Besalú lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5066 932L5139 672M5066 932L5053 958"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5139 672h0M5053 958h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5066 932h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5066 932h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Besalú. <a href="/atlas?year=994&amp;focus=county-of-besalu">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
